 "result_text": "Equation fields now use Knack's own formatted value for `.formatted`. For the issue's example, `field_377` should give `4` instead of `372171.318\u2026`. The raw value is still available through `.raw`. I haven't run the code or any tests.\n\n- **`knackpy/models.py`:** I added `\"equation\": {\"use_knack_format\": True}` to `FIELD_SETTINGS`. `Record` now passes Knack's formatted value to the field, and the default formatter returns it unchanged.\n- **`knackpy/fields.py`:** The old check treated a formatted value of `0` as missing and fell back to the raw value. For an equation in days, that would have returned the raw seconds, so the check now only falls back when the formatted value is `None`. This also applies to the other fields that use Knack's format: `name`, `timer` and `id`.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
